# CampusPulse — AI provider config
# Copy this file to .env and fill in ONE of the keys below.
# The app picks the first available key in this order: Groq → Gemini → OpenRouter
# If none are set, AI features are disabled and the app works normally (graceful degradation).

# --- Option 1: Groq (recommended — fastest, free tier) ---
# Get your key at: https://console.groq.com/keys
# Free tier: Good for development and testing
# Model used: llama-3.3-70b-versatile
# Supports: categorization, priority assessment, duplicate detection, summarization
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# --- Option 2: Google Gemini (free tier) ---
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Free tier: Generous rate limits for development
# Model used: gemini-1.5-flash
# Supports: all AI features with fast responses
# GEMINI_API_KEY=AIza...

# --- Option 3: OpenRouter (fallback) ---
# Get your key at: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Supports many models, good for production
# Model used: openai/gpt-4o-mini
# Supports: all AI features via OpenAI-compatible API
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# --- Advanced: Custom timeouts (optional) ---
# Timeout for AI requests in milliseconds (default: 8000ms for suggestions, 12000ms for assistant)
# AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=8000

# --- Notes ---
# - Leave all keys commented to disable AI features (app still works perfectly)
# - AI features degrade gracefully: if API fails, fallback to keyword matching
# - No telemetry or tracking — keys are only used for API calls
# - For production: use environment variables instead of this file
#   export GROQ_API_KEY="..." && python backend/app.py
